A||||6||loafer87gt||Fixing Cracked Manifolds||||1||
Z||000000||loafer87gt||01-10-2000||02:25 AM||||Hi guys,<P>I am going to be doing some work on my engine and figured I might as well patch up my manifolds AGAIN!! They are starting to crack really badly, and I have allready repaired (welded) them twice and replaced the gasket three times. Should I just junk my manifolds or is there any way to fix the cracks permanently. ||||reg||1
Z||000001||dogtired||01-10-2000||02:38 AM||||My opinion would be to replace them, since they have been repaired that many times???<BR>I purchased a pair of reinforced flange welded from the Fiero Factory (ED Parks), then I cleaned them out and i am very happy with them. I do not remember the price off the top of my head, but I didn't want to have to do it again down the road??<BR>Good Luck!<BR>Careful with those Bolts  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/redface.gif">||||reg||6
Z||000002||Phil||01-10-2000||07:23 AM||||Make sure that the feet are flat and aligned with other also elongate the bolt holes so that the manifolds go on the block without stress.||||reg||1
Z||000003||TOM||01-10-2000||12:16 PM||||I have reinforced and ported a few pairs and never had any problems with cracks||||reg||1
Z||000004||mshill||01-12-2000||02:10 PM||||I just got my engine out and one of the things I was planning on fixing was the exhaust leak on the front manifold.  When I got it out, sure enough, the manifold is cracked at the weld on the tube NOT at the flange.<P>The other problem is that not only is it cracked around the weld, but there is also a crack perpendicular to the weld about 25% around the collector pipe.  Is this weldable or should I seek out another manifold?<P>||||reg||1
Z||000005||TOM||01-12-2000||08:17 PM||||I would weld it then fix the problem that causes them to crack.<BR>Does anyone want to know why the forward manifold cracks?<BR>It get hot the water running down the back window splashes on it causing a thermal shock. Enough of these and it cracks. <BR>There used to be a rubber strip that sealed the window to the decklid but it was removed in pontiacs infinite wisdom of it may get hot enough to melt||||reg||1
Z||000006||WKDFIRO||01-12-2000||11:45 PM||||The rubber strip will protect the manifolds as long as the trunk lid is closed. I made the mistake of putting my umbrella in the trunk. I was outside in the rain and raised the trunklid, and guess where ALL the water on the lid went! I heard a short sizzle and then a heartbreaking, teethgnashing, CRACK! Funny thing is that nothing is leaking yet but I have been to chicken to look back there.... ||||reg||9
